{
  "analysis": "The VM's memory model is now clear: word-addressed by aligned address, little-endian byte order within each 32-bit word. The ELF loader loads .text/.data/.rodata sections by name and uses the `main` symbol as entry point. The VM uses x86/Linux syscall numbers (read=0, write=1, open=2, close=3, lseek=8, time=201), not MIPS Linux numbers. This means a standard glibc binary won't work - I need a freestanding build with custom syscall wrappers and a minimal libc. The mipsel cross-compiler is installed.",
  "plan": "Check if the VM implements MFHI/MFLO (needed for division), floating-point instructions, and how doom finds the WAD file. Then I'll create a minimal libc and build script.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'mfhi\\|mflo\\|mthi\\|mtlo\\|0x12\\|0x10\\|0x11\\|0x13\\|float\\|double\\|cvt\\|sqrt\\|FCMP\\|fcmp' /app/vm.js | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -rn 'float\\|double\\|sin\\|cos\\|tan\\|sqrt\\|pow\\|floor\\|ceil\\|atof\\|strtod' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/*.c | grep -v '//' | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'DOOMGENERIC_RESX\\|DOOMGENERIC_RESY\\|DG_ScreenBuffer' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric.h /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric.c | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'doom.wad\\|DOOMWADDIR\\|IWAD\\|iwad\\|D_DoomMain\\|M_FindResponse\\|m_argv\\|FindIWAD' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/d_iwad.c /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/d_main.c | head -60\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
